      {
        "text": "And Rab-shakeh said unto them, Speak ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great king, the king of Assyria, What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:19",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou sayest, (but they are but vain words,) I have counsel and strength for the war. Now on whom dost thou trust, that thou rebellest against me?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:20",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, behold, thou trustest upon the staff of this bruised reed, even upon Egypt, on which if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so is Pharaoh king of Egypt unto all that trust on him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "Isa. 36:6; Ezek. 29:6 (6–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 68
          },
          {
            "start": 149,
            "end": 151
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:21",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye say unto me, We trust in the Lord our God: is not that he, whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah hath taken away, and hath said to Judah and Jerusalem, Ye shall worship before this altar in Jerusalem?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:22",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Now therefore, I pray thee, give pledges to my lord the king of Assyria, and I will deliver thee two thousand horses, if thou be able on thy part to set riders upon them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:23",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "How then wilt thou turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master’s servants, and put thy trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:24",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Am I now come up without the Lord against this place to destroy it? The Lord said to me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:25",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, and Shebna, and Joah, unto Rab-shakeh, Speak, I pray thee, to thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand it: and talk not with us in the Jews’ language in the ears of the people that are on the wall.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 158
          },
          {
            "start": 233,
            "end": 236
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:26",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "But Rab-shakeh said unto them, Hath my master sent me to thy master, and to thee, to speak these words? hath he not sent me to the men which sit on the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 111
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:27",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Rab-shakeh stood and cried with a loud voice in the Jews’ language, and spake, saying, Hear the word of the great king, the king of Assyria:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "2 Chr. 32:18 (5–26)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:28",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus saith the king, Let not Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you out of his hand:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:29",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the Lord, saying, The Lord will surely deliver us, and this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 18:30",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make an agreement with me by a present, and come out to me, and then eat ye every man of his own vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his cistern:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 78
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 129
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
